{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 19, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.2-3b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was the ruler of the County of Tripoli from 1149 until his death in 1152. He was a member of the Bogholar family and a descendant of Hugh I Count of Tripoli. As the ruler of the county he was involved in various conflicts with the neighboring kingdoms of Damascus and Aleppo.\n\n* **Early Life ** \nRaymond III was born around 1122 to Pagan the Elder and his wife Eremburga. He was the son of Pagan the Elder who ruled the County of Tripoli from 1112 until his death in 1145. Raymond's older brother Amalric I Count of Tripoli ruled the county from 1145 until his death in 1151. \n\n* **Reign as Count of Tripoli ** \nRaymond III ruled the County of Tripoli from 1149 until his death in 1152. He fought several battles against the Zengid dynasty of Aleppo and Damascus. One of his most notable battles was the Battle of Inab in 1149. Raymond III was also involved in the fall of the County of Tripoli to the Zengid dynasty in 1152.\n\n* **Succession to the County of Tripoli ** \nRaymond III died in 1152 without an heir. This led to a succession crisis in the County of Tripoli. Amalric I Count of Tripoli succeeded his brother as the ruler of the county but died in 1151. This led to a struggle between the young Amalric II Count of Tripoli and the Zengid dynasty.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.001581966644152999}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.0001299296854995191}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.1985016018152237}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.194758028257638e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.0002616301644593477}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -6.01988795096986e-05}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.007840453647077084}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -1.2561371326446533}, {"token": " ruler", "logprob": -0.5851150155067444}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.00025936577